# graphify: track the graph itself (graph.json, manifest.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md,
# graph.html, cost.json) so it persists across machines; ignore regenerable
# cache + machine-local hook/interpreter state (canonical block - see
# git-hooks/README.md; the post-commit hook keeps this in sync everywhere)
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/.graphify_detect.err
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
graphify-out/.commits_since_update
graphify-out/.needs_update
graphify-out/.hook_update.log
graphify-out/20*/

# Codex workspace config (track only shared config/symlinks; ignore runtime state)
.codex/*
!.codex/config.toml
!.codex/commands
!.codex/prompts

# papyrus-server build output (migrations copied from packages/local-db at build time)
apps/server/resources/

# webui build output
apps/webui/dist/

# iCloud Drive conflict copies.
#
# This repo lives under ~/Documents, which is synced by iCloud Drive (Desktop &
# Documents). When it resolves a conflict it writes a duplicate beside the
# original — "Iris 2.tsx", "socket-path 2.ts", even whole directories like
# "commands 2/". 33 of them had been committed by the time anyone noticed, and
# one ("control-plane-bridge.test 2.ts") broke @ade/webui typecheck, because
# tsc globs *.ts while bun's test runner does not glob "*.test 2.ts" — so the
# stray file was compiled but never run.
#
# This rule stops them reaching a commit. It does NOT stop them being created:
# the actual fix is to keep the working copy outside an iCloud-synced folder.
# Verified when added: zero tracked files match this pattern.
* [0-9]
* [0-9].*
